<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Additional ablation studies</h2>

<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>The data efficiency of proposed VAE structure</h3>

<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Follow the official splitting of train/validation set in nuScenes, we test the proposed VAE performance under different fraction of training data. As shown in Table <a href="#A6.T17" title="Table 17 ‣ F.1 The data efficiency of proposed VAE structure ‣ Appendix F Additional ablation studies ‣ Towards foundational LiDAR world models with efficient latent flow matching" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>, our method only need half of the training data to exceed all of previous data compressor, as we mentioned in the abstract.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A6.T17" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A6.T17.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 17</span>: </span><span id="A6.T17.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Performance of proposed VAE under different training data fraction, under 192x compression rate, 100 epochs training</span></figcaption>
<table id="A6.T17.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A6.T17.5.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A6.T17.5.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_tt">Data fraction</td>
